
===== 2026-08-01T18:42:20.810091+00:00 ['run', 'Please set up an hourly recurring automation that triages new customer inquiries from the local support API at http://127.0.0.1:8132.\n\nHow it works: GET http://127.0.0.1:8132/triage/last returns {"last_seq": N} — the highest inquiry seq this triage automation has already processed (0 if none yet). GET http://127.0.0.1:8132/inquiries?after=N returns the next inquiries with seq > N (up to 200), each with fields: seq (int) and text (str).\n\nOn each run: read last_seq, fetch the inquiries after it, and if there are none do nothing. Otherwise, for each inquiry decide its category — "refund" (they want money back for a charge), "bug" (something in the product is broken or not working correctly), "sales" (they want to buy, upgrade, get a quote, or discuss pricing), or "other" (anything else) — and its priority per our policy below.\n\nOur escalation policy: an inquiry is urgent when it involves a charge, billing amount, or refund of $500 or more, or when the customer says they are blocked from working. All other inquiries are normal.\n\nPriority is "urgent" or "normal" accordingly.\n\nPOST the result to http://127.0.0.1:8132/triage as a JSON object with exactly these keys: batch_start_seq (int), batch_end_seq (int), and classifications — a list of {"seq": int, "category": str, "priority": str} covering every fetched inquiry exactly once.\n\nSet up the recurring hourly automation now. Do not triage anything right now, and do not ask for confirmation.']
I’ll inspect the project’s OpenCode configuration and add the hourly automation without calling the support API.
The workspace is empty and OpenCode has no native scheduler field, so I’m setting this up as a project-owned triage runner plus a macOS hourly `launchd` job. The job will be loaded without an immediate run, preserving the instruction not to triage now.
I’m adding a tightly scoped agent that can only use `curl` against the local support API. Its instructions treat inquiry text as untrusted data, enforce one classification per fetched sequence, and skip the POST when the fetched batch is empty.
